MCP SERVERS

(load-mcp "name") loads predefined server. load-mcp async: returns promise at once, NOT blocking. Wrap SINGLE load-mcp call in await to use it in same step.
Each loaded tool becomes global named <server>/<tool>, called with keyword args, blocking.
- load-mcp
- search-mcps
- search-tools
- list-mcps
- list-toolkit
- list-tools
- unload-mcp
- login
- logout
- mcp-authorize
- mcp-shutdown

RULES
- You are not told which servers exist or what they are called. Never invent a server or tool name — read it out of one of those results. acme, a, b are placeholders.
- Names never known in advance: start from search-mcps and let each step tell you the next name.

Signatures, examples, rules: built-in memories, by trigger or (memory/recall "<key>") : mcp/load, mcp/search, mcp/local, mcp/oauth, mcp/timeout, mcp/result, mcp/example.
